# R2 stage0-tcc-0.9.26 byte-identity pins.  Checked from /build (CWD) by `sha256sum -c`.
# kaem --strict ABORTS HARD on any mismatch -> a build-failing byte-identity gate.
#
# !! RECORD-AT-PIN-TIME (amd64) !!  Unlike R0/R1, there is NO upstream amd64 fixed point
# for tcc-0.9.26: live-bootstrap ships ONLY x86 + riscv64 checksums (steps/tcc-0.9.26/
# *.{x86,riscv64}.checksums) because its canonical, fully-exercised bootstrap path is
# 32-bit x86 (rootfs.py default --arch x86; stage0_arch_map only maps amd64->AMD64).
# mes-0.27.1 HAS an amd64 fixed point, but tcc-0.9.26 amd64 was never pinned upstream.
# => Capture these eight sha256 values AFTER the first green amd64 CS build and paste
#    them in below.
#
# PATHS = the §D STAGING paths /build/output/usr/...  (CONTRACTS §D: the build writes
# BINDIR=/build/output/usr/bin + LIBDIR=/build/output/usr/lib/mes — NEVER /usr, which is
# read-only — and the gate runs BEFORE nothing-needs-copying, so the files are already
# at /build/output).  Absolute paths => the check is CWD-independent.
#
# CAVEAT (CONTRACTS §D self-referential refinement): tcc-mes/tcc-boot0/tcc-boot1 bake the
# STAGING libdir (/build/output/usr/lib/mes) — see tcc.kaem §LIBDIR — so their bytes also
# differ from any writable-/usr build; the DELIVERABLE tcc bakes the CONSUMER /usr/lib/mes.
# All are reproducible (OUTPUT_DIR is the fixed /build/output) and all are record-at-pin-time.
#
# PINNED 2026-06-24 — the FIRST green amd64 CS build (fix-shift cracked mescc->tcc-boot0, lb#470).
# Captured from the published artifact gs://minimalmertic-sign-staging/stage0-tcc-0.9.26-0.9.26-a/.
ac21410449a0df354c41ab0735d92d486d6d39adb460c393cda9f737ac18a36f  /build/output/usr/bin/tcc-mes
# ── RE-PINNED 2026-09-03 (tcc-boot0, tcc-boot1, tcc) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Values captured from the b802a9ad buildbot round (amd64 res-server), which printed all eight
# computed shas immediately before the gate.  Superseded values, for the record:
#   df3251355370d4007c6e807cd1cc7296fc8f194fa57a4af3ededfde1f0374a0c  tcc-boot0  (pinned 2026-06-24)
#   72be64c1271b2cfa92da057aeb9bfd26fdd75f8ad851024c7ee723ffc9040402  tcc-boot1  (pinned 2026-06-24)
#   f3f100fedd7d6a67aa67d4b1771f019c0412507e27e622cb15a6ca8557d41540  tcc        (pinned 2026-06-24)
#
# CAUSE: commit 07a8b300 repointed
# the boot-loop's `-I` from the merged /usr/include (a first-writer-wins rootfs draw that crashed
# this rung twice on buildbot) to R1's single-writer sysroot /usr/lib/mes-bedrock/include.  Those
# three are linked `-g -v -static`, and tcc-0.9.26 bakes each included header's RESOLVED path into
# its stabs debug info, so the path change moves their bytes.
#
# The change is path-only, and that is MEASURED, not assumed:
#   * tcc-mes, built by mescc whose include path was repointed IDENTICALLY, is byte-identical (OK).
#   * libc.a, libgetopt.a, crt1.o and libtcc1.a — compiled with build-tree -I paths that did NOT
#     change — are all byte-identical (OK).
#   * stage0-tcc-0.9.27 (R3) took the same repoint and its seal PASSED; its link is `-v -w -static`
#     with NO -g.  Same change, no debug info, no byte movement.
# So the delta is confined to exactly the binaries that record paths, which is the definition of a
# path-only change.  The compiler, the sources and the header CONTENT are unchanged.
#
# CORROBORATION FROM THE SAME RUN: the other FIVE pins reproduced EXACTLY, on different hardware
# and months after they were cut in June — tcc-mes ac214104…, libc.a 29168041…, libgetopt.a
# 7de27a4b…, crt1.o c746f523…, libtcc1.a 41d8eec4….  So the pipeline is still a fixed point; only
# the three -g binaries moved, and only by the length of a path string.
#
# WHAT WOULD FALSIFY THIS: if a later round fails the gate again with values different from the
# three below, the cause is NOT the path change and the rung has a real determinism problem.
# tcc.kaem prints the computed shas before every gate check, so that case is one log away.
baf9591b97fe558f4837e37fc4ea32d099544e732870c53178c64ac8b7623f0d  /build/output/usr/bin/tcc-boot0
48923b3d4c984c80e1e1de929f9ff1114e57fc12993a6a69903e59d037f6f9b6  /build/output/usr/bin/tcc-boot1
6733e8f6a012d283ce23c7f9dd4e23866d693eebb8ef4006e16d5741f0bd3447  /build/output/usr/bin/tcc
291680418bcef8d4296fd7d5b0d4a3640dc24b3caedbac3da44ca35245614e5d  /build/output/usr/lib/mes/libc.a
7de27a4ba2db3b3cf17b50ae604729ef8893fedb67243372c4eda5d22314f0f8  /build/output/usr/lib/mes/libgetopt.a
c746f523fa1427565324cb74e0adf10499474f7f512b4c70fc63c74bef5f3240  /build/output/usr/lib/mes/crt1.o
41d8eec428d29c8b575b164f1ce25b47727b858b61b14f0740c57df6655fb5dd  /build/output/usr/lib/mes/tcc/libtcc1.a
#
# NOTE: crtn.o/crti.o are EMPTY on amd64 (catm with no inputs — the x86-only branch is
# not taken), so they are not pinned (the x86 reference lists them only because the x86
# arm builds them).  tcc-0.9.26 is byte-identical to tcc (cp) so it is not separately pinned.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
